<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jimmy Carter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1924–2024</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jimmy Carter was the 39th president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, serving from 1977 to 1981. A Democrat from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, he made human rights central to foreign policy, signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torrijos-carter-treaties">Torrijos–Carter Treaties</a> with Panama in 1977 and brokered the Camp <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Accords between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and Israel in 1978, but his presidency was weakened by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> hostage crisis. He won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 2002 for his later humanitarian work.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jimmy-carter.jpg" alt="Jimmy Carter" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Department of Defense. Department of the Navy. Naval Photographic Center · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jimmy_Carter_Official_Portrait2_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
